{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The course 1.011 Project Evaluation was taught in Spring 2011 at the undergraduate level.","source_span":"1.011 | Spring 2011 | Undergraduate"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The course instructors are Prof. Joseph Sussman and Carl D. Martland.","source_span":"Prof. Joseph Sussman\nCarl D. Martland"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The 1.011 Midterm has three questions of unequal weight.","source_span":"This exam has three questions of unequal weight."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The midterm is open book and open notes; no computers or phones are allowed, but calculators and interest tables are allowed.","source_span":"OPEN BOOK, OPEN NOTES\nNo computers or phones. Calculators and interest tables are allowed."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"Question 1 of the midterm is worth 30 points total.","source_span":"Question 1 (30 points)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"Question 2 of the midterm is worth 30 points total.","source_span":"Question 2 (30 points)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"Question 3 of the midterm is worth 40 points total.","source_span":"Question 3 (40 points)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"In the Question 2 scenario, the inherited Cambridge apartment building has annual rents of $200,000 and annual operating expenses of $100,000, giving profits of $100,000.","source_span":"Annual rents total $200,000 and annual operating expenses total $100,000. So your profits are $100,000."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The real estate agent in Question 2 expects identical $100,000 profits to be earned for another 20 years.","source_span":"your real estate agent expects that identical profits will be earned for another 20 years"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"In Question 2, MIT offers to buy the apartment building for $1.5 million.","source_span":"You receive an offer from MIT to buy the building for $1.5 million"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"Question 3 is based on the article \"Decaying Dams Pose Risk, Engineers Say\" by Kyle Cheney, published in the Boston Globe on March 15, 2011.","source_span":"Cheney, Kyle. “Decaying Dams Pose Risk, Engineers Say.” Boston Globe, March 15, 2011."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"Senator Marc Pacheco proposed a bill establishing a loan program to fund cities and towns for repair or decommissioning of deteriorating dams.","source_span":"Senator Marc Pacheco has proposed a bill establishing a loan program to provide funding to cities and towns for repair or decommissioning of deteriorating dams."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The stakeholder-identification part of Question 3 (identify 5 important stakeholders) is worth 15 points.","source_span":"Identify 5 important stakeholders. Describe their interests and whether they would favor the legislation or not."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","statement":"The Question 3 task of developing a prioritized list of dams to receive funding, assuming the bill passes, is worth 16 points.","source_span":"Assume that the bill has passed and you have the task of developing a prioritized list of dams to receive funding."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[1],"question":"Who taught MIT's 1.011 Project Evaluation course in Spring 2011?","answer":"Prof. Joseph Sussman and Carl D. Martland taught the course."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What materials were students allowed to use during the 1.011 midterm exam?","answer":"The exam was open book and open notes; calculators and interest tables were allowed, but computers and phones were not."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[4,5,6],"question":"How many points was each of the three questions worth on the 1.011 midterm?","answer":"Question 1 was worth 30 points, Question 2 was worth 30 points, and Question 3 was worth 40 points."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[7,8],"question":"In the 1.011 midterm's apartment building scenario, what are the annual rents, operating expenses, and expected duration of profits?","answer":"Annual rents total $200,000 and annual operating expenses total $100,000, giving $100,000 in annual profits, which are expected to continue for another 20 years."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[9],"question":"What offer does MIT make for the inherited apartment building in Question 2 of the 1.011 midterm?","answer":"MIT offers to buy the building for $1.5 million."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[10],"question":"What newspaper article, author, and date does Question 3 of the 1.011 midterm reference?","answer":"It references Kyle Cheney's article \"Decaying Dams Pose Risk, Engineers Say,\" published in the Boston Globe on March 15, 2011."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_exams","fact_refs":[11],"question":"What legislative proposal regarding Massachusetts dams is described in the 1.011 midterm's Question 3?","answer":"Senator Marc Pacheco proposed a bill to establish a loan program funding cities and towns for repairing or decommissioning deteriorating dams."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_1-011-project-evaluation-spring-2011_syllabus","statement":"The course keyword list includes the phrase \"This changes everything\" associated with the term Game Changer.","source_span":"“This changes everything” — Game Changer"}
